# Alejandro original case schema

Import AlejandroIdentity from "./alejandro_identity.lg".
Import AlejandroJsonFields from "./alejandro_json_fields.lg".

## An AlejandroCase has:
    a caseId, which is Text.
    a tier, which is Text.
    a title, which is Text.
    an expectation, which is Text.
    a sourcePath, which is Text.
    a historical, which is Json.
## To decodeAlejandroCase (row: Json) -> Result of AlejandroCase and Text:
    Inspect alejandroOriginalCaseFields(row):
        When Err (failure):
            Return a new Err with error failure.
        When Ok (values):
            Let caseId be item 1 of values.
            Let title be item 3 of values.
            Let expectation be item 5 of values.
            Let path be item 7 of values.
            If alejandroCaseIdAccepted(caseId) is equal to false:
                Return a new Err with error "invalid original case id".
            If title is equal to "":
                Return a new Err with error "empty original title".
            If expectation is not equal to "translate" and expectation is not equal to "degrade" and expectation is not equal to "reject":
                Return a new Err with error "unknown historical expectation".
            If alejandroSourcePathAccepted(path, caseId) is equal to false:
                Return a new Err with error "invalid original source path".
            Let original be a new AlejandroCase with caseId caseId and tier (item 2 of values) and title title and expectation expectation and sourcePath path and historical row.
            Return a new Ok with value original.
    Return a new Err with error "invalid original case".
